msgid "AboutUsageSectionTitle"
msgstr "How to use"

msgid "AboutUsageText"
msgstr "Informer lives in the system tray — right-click the icon to open the menu: Notification History, Settings, About, Exit.\n\nNew notifications appear as a popup toast in the bottom-right corner. If several messages arrive close together, the ◀ ▶ arrows let you page through them without opening History, and the 🔔 bell jumps straight to the newest one. If the text doesn't fit, a \"Show full message\" button expands the toast.\n\nThe History window keeps a full list of every notification, filterable by sender, with a manual \"read\" checkbox.\n\nIn Settings you can change the interface language, history retention period, server port, whether an API key is required, the anti-spam rate limit, and which message types pop up as toasts."

msgid "AboutIntegrationSectionTitle"
msgstr "Integration"

msgid "AboutIntegrationIntro"
msgstr "Informer accepts notifications via a plain HTTP POST request with a JSON body — any system capable of sending one works (1C, scripts, third-party services)."

msgid "AboutIntegrationEndpointsTitle"
msgstr "Available endpoints:"

msgid "AboutIntegrationNote"
msgstr "The \"type\" field is optional (info/warning/error, defaults to info) — it only affects the toast's border color. The X-Api-Key header is only required if \"Require API key\" is enabled in Settings."